title: Start_Game
---
<<declare $day_count = 0>>

// Completion tracking variables
<<declare $day1_floor_done = false>>
<<declare $day1_pot_done = false>>
<<declare $day1_desk_done = false>>

<<declare $day2_carpet_done = false>>
<<declare $day2_fireplace_done = false>>
<<declare $day2_picture_done = false>>

<<declare $day3_desk_done = false>>
<<declare $day3_floor_done = false>>
<<declare $day3_fireplace_done = false>>
===
title: Diary
---
An old diary with empty pages.
Should I write something?
->Yes
->No
===
title: Book_Shelf
---
Old books covered with dust. 
Seems like no one had been using it for a long time...
Player: Uh... maybe let's not touch it. 
===
title: BR_Window
---
Player: Ew, spider web... Why is it so foggy?
Player: I can't even look outside properly...
Player: ... Hmm?
Player: There's no handle attatched to this. I can't open the window...
===
title: Blocked_Door
---
The door is blocked with wood planks.

->Open
    <<if $has_crowbar == true>>
        I can try with my crowbar... 
        (Sound of wood splintering!)
        The planks are gone. The path is clear.
        <<set $door_opened = true>>
    <<else>>
        I can't open that with my bare hands, I might need a tool.
    <<endif>>
    Player: I can't open this with my bare hands.
    Player: I might need to look for a tool...
->Ignore
    Player: It should be blocked for a reason...

===
title: Cupboard
---
You look inside the dusty cupboard.
Among the old plates, you see something heavy...
Player: I found a crowbar!
<<set $has_crowbar = true>>
===
title: Dining_Cutlery
---
There are set of cutleries...

->Take it
    Player: It's dusty, but I'll might use this somewhere.
    <<set $has_cutlery = true>>
->Leave it
===
title: Dining_Drawing
---
There is an old drawing of a man in Victorian-era clothing with black hair.
Player: It's too foggy, I can't see it well... 
===
title: Dining_Table
---
The dust on the table doesn't wipe off even when touched.
Player: How many years does it take for dust to harden like stone like this...?
===
title: Dining_Carpet
---
Player: Hmm? This is...
Player: ...
Player: ......
Player: ......!!!
Player: Blood stain?!
Player: ...... Oh.
Player: It's just a wine stain.
===
title: Dining_CleanSeat
---
Player: What a dusty table...
Player: Huh? 
Player: This spot is clean for some reason...
Player: It seems like someone had been using this seat until recently.
===
title: Cutting_Board
---
This is where the chef was slicing meat just moments ago.
Player: Is it beef for dinner tonight? Yum!
===
title: Cooking_Knife
---
It's a very sharp knife.
Player: Should I take it?

->Take it
    Player: This looks perfect to protect myself from danger...
    Chef: Hey! Hands off there!
    Player: S-Sorry, sir!
    I hurriedly put it down. I got scolded and didn't even get the knife...
->Leave it
    Well, I don't want to make any problems. 
===
title: Go_To_Sleep
---
<<if $day_count == 1 and $is_floor_left_clean and $is_pot_watered and $is_desk_cleaned_day1>>
    <<set $can_sleep = true>>
<<elseif $day_count == 2 and $is_carpet_cleaned and $is_fireplace_cleaned_day2 and $is_frame_cleaned>>
    <<set $can_sleep = true>>
<<elseif $day_count == 3 and $is_desk_cleaned_day3 and $is_floor_right_clean and $is_fireplace_cleaned_day3>>
    <<set $can_sleep = true>>
<<else>>
    <<set $can_sleep = false>>
<<endif>>

<<if $can_sleep == false>>
    Player: I can't go to sleep yet! I haven't finished all my cleaning tasks for today.
<<else>>
    Player: Should I go to sleep?
    -> Yes
        <<if $day_count < 3>>
            (You lay down and fall into a deep sleep...)
            <<set $day_count += 1>>
            Next day: Day {$day_count}.
        <<else>>
            (The three days are up. You've completed your time at the mansion...)
            The story concludes here.
        <<endif>>
    -> No
        (You decide to stay up a bit longer.)
<<endif>>
===
title: Flower_Pot
---
<<if $day_count == 1>>
    <<if $is_pot_watered == false>>
        Player: Should I water this flower for my work shift?
        -> Yes
            <<start_watering_minigame>>
            <<set $is_pot_watered = true>>
            <<jump Check_Daily_Progress>>
        -> No
            Player: I'll do it later.
    <<else>>
        Player: The flower looks healthy and watered now!
    <<endif>>
<<else>>
    Player: I don't have to clean this!
<<endif>>
===
title: Fireplace
---
<<if $day_count == 2>>
    <<if $is_fireplace_cleaned_day2 == false>>
        Player: The fireplace is cold. I should prepare some firewood.
        -> Light Fire
            <<start_fireplace_minigame>>
            <<set $is_fireplace_cleaned_day2 = true>>
            <<jump Check_Daily_Progress>>
        -> Leave it
    <<else>>
        Player: The fire is burning nicely now.
    <<endif>>

<<elseif $day_count == 3>>
    <<if $is_fireplace_cleaned_day3 == false>>
        Player: The fireplace is cold. I should prepare some firewood.
        -> Light Fire
            <<start_fireplace_minigame>>
            <<set $is_fireplace_cleaned_day3 = true>>
            <<jump Check_Daily_Progress>>
        -> Leave it
    <<else>>
        Player: The fire is burning nicely now.
    <<endif>>

<<else>>
    Player: I don't have to clean this!
<<endif>>
===
title: Office_Frame
---
<<if $day_count == 2>>
    <<if $is_frame_cleaned == false>>
        Player: This old painting is covered in thick dust.
        -> Clean Painting
            <<start_dusting_minigame>>
            <<set $is_frame_cleaned = true>>
            <<jump Check_Daily_Progress>>
        -> Leave it
    <<else>>
        Player: The portrait looks much cleaner now.
    <<endif>>
<<else>>
    Player: I don't have to clean this!
<<endif>>
===
title: Office_Desk
---
<<if $day_count == 1>>
    <<if $is_desk_cleaned_day1 == false>>
        Player: There are papers and books scattered all over the desk.
        -> Tidy up desk
            <<start_desk_minigame>>
            <<set $is_desk_cleaned_day1 = true>>
            <<jump Check_Daily_Progress>>
        -> Leave it
    <<else>>
        Player: The desk is neat and organised now.
    <<endif>>

<<elseif $day_count == 3>>
    <<if $is_desk_cleaned_day3 == false>>
        Player: There are papers and books scattered all over the desk.
        -> Tidy up desk
            <<start_desk_minigame>>
            <<set $is_desk_cleaned_day3 = true>>
            <<jump Check_Daily_Progress>>
        -> Leave it
    <<else>>
        Player: The desk is neat and organised now.
    <<endif>>

<<else>>
    Player: I don't have to clean this!
<<endif>>
===
title: Floor_Sweep_Right
---
<<if $day_count == 3>>
    <<if $is_floor_right_clean == false>>
        Player: There is dust gathered here too.
        -> Sweep floor
            <<start_floor_minigame_right>>
            <<set $is_floor_right_clean = true>>
            <<jump Check_Daily_Progress>>
        -> Leave it
    <<else>>
        Player: This spot is already clean.
    <<endif>>
<<else>>
    Player: I don't have to clean this!
<<endif>>
===
title: Floor_Sweep_Left
---
<<if $day_count == 1>>
    <<if $is_floor_left_clean == false>>
        Player: This spot needs sweeping.
        -> Sweep floor
            <<start_floor_minigame_left>>
            <<set $is_floor_left_clean = true>>
            <<jump Check_Daily_Progress>>
        -> Leave it
    <<else>>
        Player: This spot is already clean.
    <<endif>>
<<else>>
    Player: I don't have to clean this!
<<endif>>
===
title: Carpet_Interaction
---
<<if $day_count == 2>>
    <<if $is_carpet_cleaned == false>>
        Player: Something looks strange under this carpet...
        -> Flip open carpet
            <<start_carpet_minigame>>
            <<set $is_carpet_cleaned = true>>
            <<jump Check_Daily_Progress>>
        -> Leave it alone
    <<else>>
        Player: The carpet is clean and neat now. No secret mess hiding underneath!
    <<endif>>
<<else>>
    Player: I don't have to clean this!
<<endif>>
===
title: Check_Daily_Progress
---
<<if $day_count == 1 and $is_floor_left_clean and $is_pot_watered and $is_desk_cleaned_day1>>
    Player: All job is done for today! 

<<elseif $day_count == 2 and $is_carpet_cleaned and $is_fireplace_cleaned_day2 and $is_frame_cleaned>>
    Player: All job is done for today! 

<<elseif $day_count == 3 and $is_desk_cleaned_day3 and $is_floor_right_clean and $is_fireplace_cleaned_day3>>
    Player: All job is done for today! 
<<endif>>
===